  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758893,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "Prepare for a frantic, pixelated brawl in *1.000 Kung-Fu Maniacs*, a relentlessly chaotic and hilarious action game for the Commodore 64! You are the last hope against a seemingly endless horde of identically dressed, kung-fu wielding opponents. The plot is simple: survive. The challenge? Overwhelming.\n\nGameplay revolves around mastering a limited but effective set of martial arts moves – punches, kicks, and a devastating flying kick – while navigating increasingly crowded and bizarre environments. Each level throws hundreds of enemies at you simultaneously, demanding quick reflexes and strategic positioning.  Power-ups, like temporary invincibility and speed boosts, offer brief respites from the madness.\n\nThe game's charm lies in its sheer absurdity and addictive gameplay loop.  The repetitive visuals and chiptune soundtrack contribute to the frenetic atmosphere.  Can you defeat 1,000 Kung-Fu Maniacs? It's a test of endurance, skill, and your ability to laugh in the face of utter chaos. Prepare to be overwhelmed!"
    },
